# English pyramid sweepstake

Parallel game to the World Cup sweepstake. Data lives in `app/data/english-pyramid-fantasy.ts`.

## Structure

- Seven managers, **fourteen clubs each** — one **title** pick and one **survival** pick from each division at draft (Premier League → National League South). Clubs that promote/relegate keep scoring in their new division (e.g. York City drafted as NL, now League Two for 2026/27).
- **Title draft:** pre-season outright winner betting odds within each division (lower decimal = stronger favourite). Each manager gets **exactly one pick at each odds rank** (1st favourite through 7th) spread across the seven divisions — player index `p` takes rank `((p + divisionIndex) mod 7) + 1`.
- **Survival draft:** bottom 7 by relegation odds (or longest title shots where markets are thin). Complementary deal: `p` takes survival rank `((6 - p + divisionIndex) mod 7) + 1` so title-heavy managers do not also stack every relegation favourite.
- Scoring (`ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FANTASY_SCORING`): **3** home win, **4** away win, **1** draw (any score except 0–0), **−1** for a boring 0–0 (overrides draw + clean-sheet), **+1** clean sheet, **+1** for 3+ goals scored, **−1** for 3+ conceded, **+1** per red card.
- **League season only — no knockouts, no cups, no elimination.** All fourteen clubs score points all season. Do not apply World Cup bracket, knockout survival, or “teams left” logic to this game.

## Shared UI

- `EnglishPyramidFantasy.tsx` wraps `WorldCupFantasy.tsx` with pyramid data, scoring helpers, and copy. UI improvements (W/L/D on results, bonus/penalty labels on team lines, manager photo cache busting, lightbox, etc.) belong in `WorldCupFantasy.tsx` and apply to **both** sweepstakes automatically.
- Per-game scoring display uses `getTeamMatchDisplay()` from `app/lib/english-pyramid-scoring.ts` (clean sheet bonus included).

## Fixtures and kick-off times

- Maintain `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FIXTURES` with **every league match** involving our **98 clubs** (not just games between sweepstake clubs).
- Refresh the bulk schedule with `npm run english-pyramid:fetch-fixtures -- --write` (ESPN: PL → NL; Football Web Pages: NL North/South).
- **National League (tier 5)** fixtures typically publish around **10 July** each summer. `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-fixture-check.yml` polls ESPN twice daily **10–20 July** (plus weekly Mondays) and auto-commits when eng.5 fixtures appear.
- **NL North / South** come from Football Web Pages team fixture pages (`scripts/lib/english-pyramid-fwp-nln-nls.cjs`). Same fetch/check commands refresh them; kick-offs are Europe/London → UTC. If FWP returns Cloudflare 403, the fetcher falls back to BBC Sport month fixture pages.
- **League only** — cup ties (FA Cup, League Cup, etc.) are excluded automatically (season slug + single-leg pair filter; FWP filters to `national-league-north` / `national-league-south` only).
- Weekly GitHub Action `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-fixture-check.yml` compares remote sources to the repo and auto-refreshes when kick-offs move (international breaks, postponements).
- Manual drift check: `npm run english-pyramid:check-fixtures` (add `--write` to apply).
- First matchday opens on the earliest fixture date in the ledger (e.g. Championship often kicks off Friday before the main Saturday batch).
- Store `utcDate` as **UTC ISO-8601** (`2026-08-09T14:00:00Z`) converted from the **Europe/London** kick-off (handles GMT/BST).
- Typical UK kick-offs: **12:30**, **15:00**, **17:30** (weekend), **19:45** / **20:00** (midweek). Full-time is usually ~115 minutes later.
- Fixture ids: stable keys such as `2026-08-09-ars-che` (date + home code + away code).
- When recording a result, roll fixtures forward — add the next known upcoming sweepstake fixture(s) so the UI keeps showing what is next.

## Manual / agent score updates

When asked to update English pyramid scores (or by the scheduled GitHub workflow):

- Append finished **league** matches to `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_MANUAL_MATCHES` only — one ledger for all seven divisions.
- Only look for **newly finished** games not already in the manual ledger. Do not re-verify recorded entries.
- Use team codes from `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_TEAM_BY_CODE` / `getEnglishPyramidTeamSearchTerms()` (club name variants for matching).
- Check reliable UK sources: BBC Sport, Sky Sports, official league/club sites, Flashscore.
- Add only final results: home/away teams (`tla` code), final goals, red-card tallies (including second-yellow dismissals).
- Cross-check red-card tallies against ESPN before finishing any score update: run `npm run english-pyramid:validate` (includes `scripts/english-pyramid-validate-red-cards.cjs`). If ESPN reports reds for a finished ledger match and the ledger is lower, fix the ledger before pushing.
- When appending a new manual result, always set explicit `homeRedCards` and `awayRedCards` (use `0` when none). Never omit the fields.
- **Every manual result must exist in `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FIXTURES` with matching home/away TLAs.** The full-season fixture list is kept in-repo (unlike the rolling World Cup schedule), so `npm run english-pyramid:validate` fails if the ledger and fixtures drift apart or if a fixture is overdue with no result.
- Do not hand-edit standings — `computeStandings()` in `app/lib/english-pyramid-scoring.ts` derives totals.
- After any ledger change, run `npm run english-pyramid:standings` and use that output as the only source for totals and leader/bottom wording in `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FANTASY_DAILY_UPDATE`.
- Refresh `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FANTASY_DAILY_UPDATE` when the table changes. Tone: **foul-mouthed Grok / Tesla cabin energy** — sweary, rude, British football roast, genuinely funny. Name managers and clubs. Avoid repeating the same gag. Still mirror standings totals exactly; do not invent scores.
- Push to **`origin/main`** unless the user asks for PR-only work.

## Scheduled workflow

- **Scores:** `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-score-agent.yml` runs `npm run english-pyramid:sync` for due fixtures on ESPN tiers (PL → NL) and **Football Web Pages for NL North/South**. Matchday sweeps may still need the Cursor agent for roast copy / edge cases.
- **NL North / South results:** same sync job scrapes FWP team fixture pages (kick-off cells become `1 - 0` when final). Red cards are recorded as `0` from FWP tables (not exposed reliably there) — cross-check Flashscore/BBC if a dismissal is reported.
- **Due fixtures:** `scripts/english-pyramid-due-fixtures.cjs` keeps fixtures due until recorded (no lookback expiry), with a matchday sweep fallback for same-day games.
- **Due fixtures:** `scripts/english-pyramid-due-fixtures.cjs` keeps fixtures due until recorded (no lookback expiry), with a matchday sweep fallback for same-day games.
- **Health check:** `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-health-check.yml` runs `npm run english-pyramid:validate` on a fixed schedule and fails loudly on overdue fixtures or ESPN red-card drift.
- **Validate split:** `npm run english-pyramid:validate:scores` (ledger + reds), `npm run english-pyramid:validate` (same — no separate roast validator yet).

`.github/workflows/english-pyramid-score-agent.yml` runs on UK matchday windows (Europe/London), not US World Cup hours:

- **Weekends**: frequent checks ~14:10–22:50 London for 12:30 / 15:00 / 17:30 / evening KO batches.
- **Midweek**: checks ~21:00–22:50 London for 19:45 / 20:00 KOs.
- `scripts/english-pyramid-due-fixtures.cjs` decides when to trigger based on fixture kick-offs + 115 minute delay, with a matchday sweep fallback.

## Example Slack / agent prompt

> Sync English pyramid sweepstake scores. Find newly finished matches for our 98 clubs across PL → NL South, append to `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_MANUAL_MATCHES`, refresh fixtures and daily roast, merge to main, push origin/main.
